~ Deferred values — `io.@readStdin` (see docs/concurrency/README.md).
~ `io.@readStdin()` is a value-returning leaf IO primitive: it LAUNCHES a stdin line read in
~ the background and hands back a DEFERRED Text immediately. The value threads through the
~ `line` binding untouched (promise pipelining); the fiber only WAITS (forces) at the first
~ strict operation that reads its bytes — here the `==` behind `equals`.

<< core.io
<< core.test

^ = () -> Num => <
  line = io.@readStdin()      ~ launches the read, returns a deferred Text (no wait here)
  assert(line, equals("no loops, only recursion and regret"))     ~ FORCES the value
  0
>
